![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The test is named `record_only_error_observation_keeps_goal_active`, but it never actually invokes `on_turn_error` on the lifecycle contributors. As a result, the error is never observed by the goal extension, making this a vacuous test that passes without executing the target code path. We should invoke `on_turn_error` on the contributors to properly test the error handling behavior.

```rust
    let observed_error = CodexErrorInfo::UsageLimitExceeded;
    for contributor in registry.turn_lifecycle_contributors() {
        contributor
            .on_turn_error(codex_extension_api::TurnErrorInput {
                turn_id: "turn-1",
                error: &observed_error,
                session_store: &session_store,
                thread_store: &thread_store,
            })
            .await;
    }
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Using `tempdir.keep()` prevents the temporary directory from being cleaned up, which leaks temporary files on disk after the test runs. Since `runtime` is declared after `tempdir`, it will be dropped first at the end of the scope, meaning `tempdir` will safely remain alive for the entire test duration. We can use `tempdir.path().abs()` instead to ensure the directory is automatically cleaned up when the test finishes.

```suggestion
    let tempdir = TempDir::new()?;
    let runtime = codex_state::StateRuntime::init(
        codex_state::SqliteConfig::new_for_testing(tempdir.path().abs()),
        "diagnostic-provider".to_string(),
    )
```
